defklown wrote:
> It was a rock piercer. Indubitably. I'm also a little curious as to why
> the monster started as a cockatrice, then became a rock piercer, then
> left a flesh golem corpse.

That's a chameleon. Shapeshifters in Nethack are powerful, in that their
changed forms have all the abilities of the real thing. Normally, if you
see an absurdly strong monster before you reach the levels they're
supposed to be appearing, it's a chameleon or a bones file.

You can prevent shapeshifters morphing into powerful attackers by
wearing a ring of protection against shapeshifters. This makes them
unable to change from their native form, which is weak.

The vanishing dagger is also weird, though.

You remember incorrectly. Rock piercers cannot pick up objects, and are
carnivores. Rock _moles_ are metallivores. See the monster reference
manual here
http://www.juiblex.co.uk/nethack/VernonSpoilers/MonsterManual/contents.html.
